+# Mobile claim status and release history (phase 5)
+
+Apply `mobile-v4.patch` to backend `42b4552`, then `mobile-claims.patch`. No new dependencies or migrations are required. This local extension is not merged or deployed upstream.
+
+`GET /api/v1/mobile/beneficiaries/me/wallet` authenticates the existing beneficiary mobile session. Staff JWTs are rejected. Ownership is derived from the session, never a query parameter. The response is private/no-store and contains:
+
+- `wallet`: existing account ID, balance, currency, status and last transaction timestamp, or null. Reading does not create an account.
+- `currentClaim`: the earliest eligible published assignment selected by the existing overview rules, or null. Before verification its ID is null and status is `not_claimed`; amount comes from the allocation. A matching saved claim supplies its actual status.
+- `claims`: own saved claim history, including closed-event records. Each record has IDs, status, method, assigned Manila session date, actual allocation value, program ID/code/name, verification/claim/release timestamps, delivery mode, released package name/unit/quantity, receipt number/issue time, and a boolean review indicator.
+- `transactions`: own claim-linked BENEFIT_CREDIT/BENEFIT_REVERSAL ledger entries. Credit amounts are positive; reversals are negative. Transaction, wallet, claim, allocation and schedule ownership must match. Transfer history and wallet writes are outside this phase.
+
+Physical release is represented only as a claim and never synthesized as a wallet credit. VERIFIED means identity checks are complete; CLAIMED plus PHYSICAL_GOODS is shown as Released. PENDING, REJECTED and VOIDED are preserved. Receipt metadata identifies the staff receipt; the mobile app does not generate a staff receipt or expose its raw snapshot.
+
+Responses exclude QR credentials/hashes, biometrics, signatures, staff attribution/contact details, release notes/evidence references, dispute text and internal receipt snapshots. An active dispute or duplicate flag produces only `needsReview: true`. A repeatable-read transaction keeps the summary internally consistent. History is currently unpaginated; add cursor pagination before a large pilot.
+
+## Verify
+
+Run `npm.cmd run test:shared` from the mobile checkout against a separate migrated database (set DATABASE_URL to that test instance). The actual TypeScript client and Express API exercise unauthenticated/staff rejection, scheduled placeholders, QR-only VERIFIED versus combined PENDING, facilitator release, receipt issuance, closed history, staff status changes, review flags, signed synthetic ledger fixtures, owner isolation, DTO allowlists, no GET-created wallet, and logout. Synthetic ledger fixtures test read mapping; they are not a claim of end-to-end simulated settlement verification.
+
+For a manual check, sign in to mobile as the test beneficiary and open Wallet > Refresh records after staff release/receipt issuance. Claim history should show Released, the recorded package/quantity, release time and receipt number. A physical-only account may correctly have no wallet account or transactions. No real goods or funds move during this local test.
